From: Ely Office
Subject: Writer comment deletions are not tracked under LOK

- With track changes on, deleting all comments in an unsaved or ODF
  document recorded each comment as a tracked deletion, so the
  tracked changes grew and the comments stayed in the file inside
  them (#148). A .docx already deleted them untracked, as Word does.
- Under LOK every format now deletes comments untracked, whether one
  thread or all of them.

diff --git a/sw/source/uibase/docvw/PostItMgr.cxx b/sw/source/uibase/docvw/PostItMgr.cxx
--- a/sw/source/uibase/docvw/PostItMgr.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/uibase/docvw/PostItMgr.cxx
@@ -1700,7 +1700,9 @@
 {
     if (!mpWrtShell->IsRedlineOn())
         return {}; // No track changes - no need to disable it
-    if (isOwnFileFormat(mpView->GetDocShell()->GetMedium()))
+    // Under LOK comments go untracked, as in Word.
+    if (!comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive()
+        && isOwnFileFormat(mpView->GetDocShell()->GetMedium()))
         return {}; // Format is smart enough to handle deleted comments in redlines
 
     return std::unique_ptr<CommentDeleteFlagsRestore>(
